{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793205935,"nonce":"O/WVEh2grMIaoeCOtgF71ygCTMI=","title":"Use independent Ash optimization controls for app preview builds","message":"Ash now supports separate AIR, LLVM IR and machine codegen optimization controls. Browser app previews should keep optimized IR while using faster machine code generation instead of the default expensive codegen pass.\n\nUse -O3 --codegen-opt-level 0 in the editable Ash-backed HashLink preview defaults. Keep saved build flags authoritative, leave other compiler/framework profiles and editor distribution builds alone, and keep optimization-only changes in the runner stage so valid Haxe bytecode is reusable.\n\nVerify the actual Pocket Studio preview through a session using the current Ash CLI, first-frame rendering, cached rebuild, app interaction and the shared run planner checks. Record observed compiler times and artifact tradeoffs here rather than in source comments.","files":null}]}